# The reason a call to the machine failed, as a message tells it (design.md
# §4.17, §1.12; defects 134, 346 and d-lane-blocking-small2-1, 2026-11-25).
#
# **A reason is the one the failed call set, read at once.** The runtime
# keeps one per thread for the filesystem (`hero_fs_why`) and one for the
# runs it starts (`hero_run_why`), and every call clears its own on the way
# in, so a reason read after any other question of the machine is that
# question's: `heroes build -o app/main.hero/b` was told *the operating
# system's own reason is 0* because the link asked again after `mkdir` had
# failed and what stands in the way had been asked of each part of the
# path, each question clearing it; through a link that loops, the same read
# told a question's refusal, *the runtime refused it before the system was
# asked*, for `mkdir`'s. So a failure carries its reason in its message from
# the line after the call (`process.made_dir`), and this module is the one
# place that words a number.
#
# **0 is no reason**: it is what a call that succeeded leaves. A refusal
# that reads 0 was told after another question, or by a runtime door that
# set none, and says that no reason was kept rather than a false one; below
# 0 the runtime refused before asking the system, told as its own since
# defect 346.
#
# Its own module, below `cli/process` and `cli/stands`, which both tell a
# reason, so it uses nothing.

extern "hero_os.h"
    function hero_fs_why() -> i64

# The clause a refusal of a filesystem call ends with, asked on the line
# after the call that failed.
function because() -> str
    return ": " + told(hero_fs_why())

# The number `because` tells, for a caller whose sentence words it with
# `told`, asked as `because` is, on the line after the call.
function last() -> i64
    return hero_fs_why()

# A reason, `hero_fs_why`'s or a run's `why`, as a message says it.
function told(why: i64) -> str
    if why < 0
        return "the runtime refused it before the system was asked, for the reason the system numbers " + (0 - why).to_str()

    if why == 0
        return "no reason was kept"
    return "the operating system's own reason is " + why.to_str()

## Tests

# Defect d-lane-blocking-small2-1: a reason is the failed call's, and a 0 is
# never told as one.
test "a reason is told as the system's, the runtime's, or as none kept, and 0 is never a reason (defect d-lane-blocking-small2-1)"
    assert told(13) == "the operating system's own reason is 13"
    assert told(-63) == "the runtime refused it before the system was asked, for the reason the system numbers 63"
    assert told(0) == "no reason was kept"

    # A call that succeeded leaves 0, so a reason asked after it is none:
    # the reason a refusal tells is read on the line after its own call.
    _ = hero_fs_why()
    assert because() == ": " + told(hero_fs_why())
